# Built plugin artifacts. Each plugin's Makefile builds its binary to the plugin directory and
# packages into dist/; both are outputs, not sources. Committing them would put ~20MB of
# platform-specific binary per plugin into the history — and a stale one would be worse than
# none, since `make package` copies whatever is there.
dist/
*/dist/

# The built binaries, by the executable name each plugin's manifest declares.
/webhook-plugin/webhook
/first-blood-plugin/first-blood
/regex-flag-plugin/regex-flag
/oidc-plugin/oidc
/plugin-template/my-plugin
